## Quick command reference

```bash
# Feature work
git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name

# Dev testing
npx expo start --dev-client --tunnel
npx expo start --dev-client --lan

# Rebuild dev clients (native changes)
npx eas-cli build --platform android --profile development
npx eas-cli build --platform ios --profile development --clear-cache

# iOS TestFlight / App Store binary
eas build --platform ios --profile production
eas submit --platform ios --latest

# Android production (local EAS; GitHub Actions mirror these)
npx eas-cli build --platform android --profile production
npx eas-cli build --platform android --profile production-play

# Credentials (Expo)
npx eas-cli credentials -p ios
```

**Android production APK:** After merge to **`main`**, wait for **Auto Version Bump**, then run **Android Production Build** manually; download the APK from the **EAS** build for that run (or publish a **GitHub Release** yourself if you want a stable link).

**Android Play AAB:** Same sequence, but run **Android Play Bundle (AAB)**; download the **.aab** from **EAS** and upload it to a **Play Console** test or production release.

